# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm project configuration — read by every install, including Vercel's.
#
# `cache` (not `cache-dir`). Vercel's build image exports
# `npm_config_cache_dir`, and npm 11+ rejects that as an unknown key:
#
#   npm warn Unknown env config "cache-dir". This will stop working in the next
#   major version of npm.
#
# The value was never honoured anyway — `cache-dir` is not an npm setting, it is
# a leftover from the pnpm-oriented parts of the image. It is also not ours to
# unset: it arrives from the build environment, so the fix is to pin the
# *supported* key here so the effective cache location is explicit and does not
# depend on which unhonoured variable the image happens to export. Setting it in
# the project is the only lever a repository has over this warning.
#
# Nothing else belongs here. In particular there is no `ignore-scripts`: that
# would suppress every dependency lifecycle script as a side effect and silently
# starve native packages, which is exactly what `allowScripts` in package.json
# exists to do deliberately and per-package.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cache=~/.npm
